WEBVTT

00:00:00.091 --> 00:00:02.725
Learn is your read-only reference library.

00:00:02.725 --> 00:00:05.531
Follow HLD from requirements to architecture,

00:00:05.531 --> 00:00:07.953
and LLD from responsibilities to Java contracts.

00:00:12.086 --> 00:00:15.409
Use Companies to study twenty proposed designs. Uber

00:00:15.409 --> 00:00:19.216
connects location freshness, spatial discovery, exclusive assignment and

00:00:19.216 --> 00:00:22.532
trip state. Published context is separated from our proposal.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.431
Open Practice to edit a graph

00:00:25.431 --> 00:00:28.718
and write decisions. Start with scope, workload

00:00:28.718 --> 00:00:31.343
assumptions, an invariant and one bottleneck prediction.

00:00:36.086 --> 00:00:38.574
Keep the same seed, traffic profile and failure

00:00:38.574 --> 00:00:42.029
setting. Run a baseline, pin it, change one

00:00:42.029 --> 00:00:46.028
input and rerun. Compare successful throughput, latency and errors.

00:00:48.087 --> 00:00:51.329
Inject a bounded outage. Inspect sampled node history

00:00:51.329 --> 00:00:55.078
and request traces, then export the experiment. This model

00:00:55.078 --> 00:00:57.883
does not prove payment correctness or exclusive driver assignment.

00:01:00.086 --> 00:01:03.652
Use Design Studio to capture requirements, capacity, HLD,

00:01:03.652 --> 00:01:07.465
API, data model and LLD. Export your browser-local

00:01:07.465 --> 00:01:11.682
bundle. Practice offers rule-based feedback. AI is disabled.
